ContractFolders sets "how buying works" as the folders a buyer is handed: each row a limestone folder with its subject on the tab and a sheet inside listing what the linked page covers, the link as a full-width row under it.

- On the site: a `spec` block with `"look": "contract-folders"` (renderer `assets/src/blocks/look-contract-folders.js`), cmp-quality "How buying from us works". Origin: pass 12 concept 243 (`243-p12-cmp-quality-buying.png`: a tabbed terms folder and an onboarding sheet with a signature line and pen, a link under each). Replaces TermsSheet on that page; TermsSheet stays in the library. Not copied from the concept: the statuses beside the onboarding codes (invented), the codes themselves, the empty pages and micro-text tab labels.
- Variants by position: the first folder (and every other one after it) is a tabbed divider set: each item a ruled line with an index tab numbered 01, 02 … on the sheet's right edge. The second (and every other one after it) is a form: each paper a ruled line with an empty mark box, the row's note under them, a signature line and a pen. Nothing is filled in: marks and signature stay empty (the statuses live on the linked page).
- Markup: `<div class="aq-contract-folders">` > `ol.__list` > `li.__f.is-tabs|.is-form` > `__folder[data-theme=light]` (`h3.__tab` > `__n`, subject; `__sheet` > `p.__k` (the second column's name), `ul.__items` > `li` > [`__ix`] `__it` [`i.__ld` dotted leader, `i.__box`], `p.__m` note, [`__sign` > `i.__sl`, `svg.__pen` > `path.__pb`, `path.__pd`]) + `p.__go` > link.
- Fields (a spec block): `h`, `intro`, `cols [subject, what the page covers, note]`, `rows [{p, v ("a · b · c"), m, link, link_label}]`.
- Tokens: folder and tab `limestone` with an `on-limestone-muted` edge and `on-limestone` subject (19 px); sheet `surface-raised` with a `paper-dim` offset shadow; items 15 px `ink` between `line` rules; tabs `surface-raised` / `surface-sunken` alternating with 12 px mono numbers; mark boxes 12 px square, 1 px `ink-subtle`, on a dotted `line-strong` leader (printed form boxes, not UI checkboxes); signature line `ink`; pen line art in `flow`; link row 16 px `action` with a mono arrow, at least 44 px, `line-strong` rule. Desktop: the folders in a row stretch to one height (the shorter cover runs deeper below its sheet), so the link rows line up. Dark: the folder carries `data-theme="light"` so the sheet stays paper inside the limestone cover; the link row follows the page theme.
- Hover / focus: the sheet lifts 4 px and the tabs fan out (each 1 px further than the one above), their numbers in `flow`; the link's arrow moves 4 px.
- Phone (860 px container or less): the folders stack; each sheet's items run in two columns at 14 px (tabs become inline numbers, mark boxes stay); the link is a 48 px row. No PhoneKit: two short lists, nothing to pick between.
- Motion (`motion.js`): ported from Subframe Motion "Archive folder" (archive-folder), MIT: the folder rises 12 px (0.42 s) and the sheet comes up out of it from a 1.5 degree tilt (0.48 s), both on a strong ease-out (0.16, 1, 0.3, 1); the items land 0.05 s apart, the tabs slide out of the sheet's edge, the signature line draws and the pen settles. Folders 0.15 s apart on desktop, each on its own scroll-in on phones. Reduced motion: the open pose.
- Not for: a table of terms with values to compare (TermsSheet, SpecTable) or a document set delivered with a system (DocList).
